Z||000000||KissMySSFiero||02-22-2001||10:42 PM||||has anyone here installed power door locks on a car from scratch.  i did a search but got frustrated cuz im tired and cant hardly read the screen.  what kinda stuff would i need to get.  ive got all i need for power mirrors and have windows already.  how simple is it.  how much time would it take a decent tech.  TIA<P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:KissMySSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:KissMySSFiero@netzero.net">KissMySSFiero@netzero.net</A>   <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">       <BR>"There's a fine line between love and beer"<BR><A HREF="http://expage.com/kissmyssfiero" TARGET=_blank>KissMySSFiero.mywebsite.hehe</A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||tgowens||02-23-2001||01:41 AM||||we just installed power locks on a Formula here in the shop........you need the actuators, the wiring harness and the lock switches.........it's a good half day job but well worth it in my book!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Haze_Performance||02-23-2001||04:37 AM||||This is my next project for the 87... Im spoiled, my 85 has power.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> When I get in the 87 I just look at the door like an fool! (DANM NO POWER!!) lol  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif"> </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>PFF Members Photo Page</A><BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1431213" TARGET=_blank><BR>Photopoint Gallery</A>||||reg||14
Z||000003||Carrolles||02-23-2001||07:14 AM||||You'll also need the relay.<P>I am preparing to add power locks and power windows to my 85se.  Strange thing is that it already has power mirrors.<P>I got a pair of donor doors to strip the goodies from.||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroJoe||02-23-2001||10:33 AM||||I just got done adding power locks and mirrors to mine on monday.  In addition to the actuators, and 3 wiring harnesses (2 doors, 1 cross car[with relay]), you'll need two steel brackets that the actuators must work with in order to move the lock rod.  If you cant get the parts off of a car yourself, it isnt that hard to install by looking in the pictures in a book.<P>As for the mirrors, again, it is 3 harnesses (2 door, 1 cross car again)  Its real simple, you just have to make sure that the connectors that plug from the cross car harness to the door harness, and then to the mirrors themselves, have the same color connectors, there were black and then white ones, and they dont plug into each other.<P>Another note on wiring harnesses, if you are going to install this into your Forumla, make sure that you get the cross car wiring harness from a Fiero with the 3rd brake light, otherwise there are two connectors from existing dash harnesses in your Fiero that will not go together.<P>Removing the dash makes things much easier, by the way.<P>If you need some pics, email me and I'll send you some of whatever you need.<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
